# L §6.1 What same does: "A thing's entries are such facts: an entry only one side states stands, and on a day on which
# the two sides' entries into one kind disagree, whatever depends on the thing being alive there is a HOLE-SAME hole (in
# a binding over that kind, an unknown member, §5.11)"; L §5.3 a later `replace` entry restates the lifespan. ana enters
# konto and later ends it with September (v2, known by the cut); ben's konto lives on. In June both sides hold it alive
# and it counts once (n_jun); in October they disagree: an unknown member, the HOLE-SAME hole naming ana's entry (a.v2)
# and ben's place (n_oct). Alone: ana 0, ben 1 (a.q, b.q). (Was REFCORE-NOT-YET: same of a place entered 2 times.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "8018e21cfbc93b9993b14456fc33abfcdb3c8ee2c077fab519ec675b7fa0600f"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "8d4353dd3d6605654f3def4ff1e56dbf6834964b26ac5d70b9e1094c80bd0fb2"
  same a.konto = b.konto

ask n_jun: count(x in accounts on 2026-06-01)
ask n_oct: count(x in accounts on 2026-10-01)
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

version v1
  cite s
  known 2025-12-01
  accounts + [konto] PLN lives 2026-01-01..

version v2
  cite s
  known 2026-01-03
  replace accounts + [konto] PLN lives 2026-01-01..2026-09-30

ask q: count(x in accounts on 2026-10-01)
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

ask q: count(x in accounts on 2026-10-01)
=== expect n_jun n_oct a.q b.q
n_jun: 1
  cut 2026-01-05
n_oct: ?"a.konto and b.konto are one, but the entry into accounts differs on 2026-10-01: 2026-01-01..2026-09-30 (a.v2) and 2026-01-01.. (b.konto)" (a.konto, b.konto)
  cut 2026-01-05
a.q: 0
  cut 2026-01-05
b.q: 1
  cut 2026-01-05
